{
 "about": "Per-weight prices (bits) of an updated weight by class, measured on OLMo-2 7B and 13B (AdamW, dense) at early, mid and late stage 1, theta_t -> theta_{t+1000}, for benchmarks/nci/covering_priced.py --prices. points: the `fwd` set (the decoder holds theta rounded to the format), what a registration of the weights alone gives. points_optimizer: the `master` set (it also holds theta's fp32 master copy), the lesser of fwd's codecs and master's; OLMo-2 publishes no Adam moments, so a registration that also covers the optimizer state prices at most this. Keys are HF tensor names (q/k/v/gate/up average into covering's roles; `named` is the cheapest of q, k, v, o, gate, up, down). cheapest: the uniform forms' c_w tiers, theta-selectable (class x theta's exponent, tables.py's theta_cheapest) over the block matrices q, k, v, o, gate, up, down (K2's M* holds no LM head, embedding or norm gamma); `theta+head` tiers are the artifact's own, which also admit lm_head and the norms. No Adam-v tier: no optimizer state is published.",
